      "writtenOn": "2019-12-04T19:01:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If you do programmedSubs.get(connectPoint) it will give you all the uniTagInfo for that connectPoint -- some of them may have been programmed, and some of them not programmed. What I am saying is that we should ONLY show those uniTagInfo for the subs programmed on this connectPoint. Which means that we need to change the programmedSubs map to be something like\nMap\u003cConnectPoint, List\u003cUniTagInformation\u003e\u003e",
      "parentUuid": "4f26c29c_5b77978b",
      "revId": "4874d8cba781fa8cf260bdc22963350cd7824723",
      "serverId": "2a2bfe1b-c5c2-48ed-9ac8-16438ab24388",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0e01adb1_4d484d3b",
        "filename": "app/src/main/java/org/opencord/olt/impl/Olt.java",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 347,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000068
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-11-28T01:54:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "My fundamental problem is here. Note that this method used to be only for creating \"TransparentFlows\". After going through the DT workflow, it appears to me that the only use case for transparent flows is in the DT FTTB use case, and only for the DPU single-tag management traffic. Which means that every other DT flow is going to be \"non-transparent\" ie it will require some modification rules, some push and set or set-vlan traffic at the OLT.\n\nYou have now modified this api for two purposes\n1) to be able to select a specific item in the uniTagList -- by providing the stag/ctag/techprofileid to find that item from the list -- which is good -- we need this api\n\nbut\n2) you are also still using the same api to do transparent flow by using the \"enableTransparentFlows\" flag - this is not good because when this flag is set, then all flows will become transparent flows and we don\u0027t want that. Only a specific flow is supposed to be transparent -- we should remove this flag, and find a way to express the need for the transparent flow via the sadis uniTaglist item.",
      "revId": "4874d8cba781fa8cf260bdc22963350cd7824723",
      "serverId": "2a2bfe1b-c5c2-48ed-9ac8-16438ab24388",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "81597011_50094211",
        "filename": "app/src/main/java/org/opencord/olt/impl/Olt.java",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 347,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000405
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-12-02T08:19:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "For DT use-case, provisionSubscriber(connectPoint) API can be used to install regular flows. Or does the use-case need to use provisionSubsriber(cTag, sTag, tpId) specifically?",
      "parentUuid": "0e01adb1_4d484d3b",
      "revId": "4874d8cba781fa8cf260bdc22963350cd7824723",
      "serverId": "2a2bfe1b-c5c2-48ed-9ac8-16438ab24388",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "add442a6_9c6bbd13",
        "filename": "app/src/main/java/org/opencord/olt/impl/Olt.java",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 347,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000068
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-12-04T19:01:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think there should only be two apis\n1) provisionSubscriber(connectPoint) \nwhich will program all the UniTagInformation in the UniTagList for that connectpoint\n2) provisionSubscriber(portname, cTag, sTag, tpid)\nwhich will program only a particular uniTagInformation in the uniTagList for the portname/connectpoint.\nIf the stag/ctag/tpid is not provided then this api becomes like the first api, except portname is provided and not the connectpoint.\n\nAll 3 operators should be able to use either of these APIs - one for bulk programming, one for specific item programming. We should not use or need special flag and like \"enableTransparentFlows\" \n\nI am still working with Amit on what the flows should look like for DT use cases -- let me send an email to you both describing the issue later today, but regardless, I strongly believe there should not be any special flag usage",
      "parentUuid": "81597011_50094211",
      "revId": "4874d8cba781fa8cf260bdc22963350cd7824723",
      "serverId": "2a2bfe1b-c5c2-48ed-9ac8-16438ab24388",
      "unresolved": false
    },
